  "reason": "Evidence: config_006 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) is the current best at 0.7250, and scvi_n200 is clearly superior to scgpt (0.725 vs 0.520). Weighted fusion edges out concat (0.725 vs 0.721). The largest untested architectural variable is the image encoder: all three completed experiments used imagenet_vit_l, so we have no evidence whether resnet50 might be competitive or superior. Question: config_038 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted) is a clean single-variable A/B test against config_006, changing only the image encoder. This directly clarifies whether the larger ViT-L backbone is necessary or whether a lighter ResNet50 could match/exceed it, which would reshape the remaining 6-experiment search space. Rationale: With 6 experiments left, resolving the image encoder question now is the highest-information experiment—it either confirms imagenet_vit_l (letting us focus on aggregation/profile refinements) or reveals resnet50 as a better base (opening a new promising branch to exploit)."
}

